From bfc74636a4599161faecad7a16d11adc8f6c2046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 05:31:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/20] avcodec/ppc: H.264 chroma + intra loop filters and
 chroma_mc4 AltiVec (O1)

Fills the remaining H.264 deblock gaps on PPC (only the luma inter
loop filters were previously vectorised) and adds the 4-wide chroma
motion compensation kernel.

libavcodec/ppc/h264dsp.c:
- h264_{v,h}_loop_filter_chroma_altivec (inter): reuses the existing
  boundary-strength mask (h264_deblock_mask) and the luma p0/q0 delta
  macro (h264_deblock_p0_q0) verbatim -- the chroma delta formula
  av_clip(((q0-p0)*4+(p1-q1)+4)>>3,-tc,tc) is identical to luma's, and
  that macro already folds the block mask into tc0masked so tc==0 lanes
  are left untouched. Chroma tc == tc0[i] (not tc0[i]+1) and lanes with
  tc0<=0 are skipped, matching h264dsp_template.c. tc0[] has one entry
  per pair of samples (inner_iters==2) so each byte is duplicated twice.
- h264_{v,h}_loop_filter_chroma_intra_altivec: p0'=(2p1+p0+q1+2)>>2,
  q0'=(2q1+q0+p1+2)>>2 under the same mask, done in s16.
- h264_{v,h}_loop_filter_luma_intra_altivec: full two-branch intra
  filter (strong p2..q2 rewrite / weak p0,q0) computed on both unpacked
  halves in s16 and selected with vec_sel on mask/ap/p2/q2 masks.
- New helpers: store8_altivec (8-wide RMW store that preserves the
  adjacent 8 bytes, same idiom as h264pred.c st8()); readAndTranspose16x8
  (readAndTranspose16x6 extended to emit columns 6 and 7, needed for
  p3/q3); TRANSPOSE_8x4_LOAD (8-row x 4-col transpose for the horizontal
  chroma edge). The horizontal chroma stores go through per-row scalar
  writes; the horizontal luma-intra writes its six modified columns with
  two overlapping write16x4() calls so nothing outside [pix-3,pix+2] is
  touched. All transposed loads use unaligned_load(), recomputing the
  alignment shift per row (no stride % 16 assumption), the same
  correctness rule as the recent vp8/vp9 vertical-MC fixes.
- Chroma filters are gated on chroma_format_idc <= 1 (the 4:2:2 variants
  keep the C path), matching the other arches.

libavcodec/ppc/h264chroma_template.c + _init.c:
- put/avg_h264_chroma_mc4_altivec (pixels_tab[1]). Computes the full
  A/B/C/D bilinear form (the C special-cases for B/C/D==0 are pure
  micro-optimisations; the arithmetic is identical and the zeroed terms
  make the extra src reads harmless), reusing OP_U8_ALTIVEC for the
  put/avg split. dst is 4-aligned in every caller, so the result is
  written a word at a time with vec_ste.

Pure AltiVec C intrinsics only -- no inline asm, so nothing here depends
on gas/Darwin assembler conventions; identical source builds for
powerpc-apple-darwin and powerpc-linux.

VALIDATED under the cross-PPC/qemu harness (qemu-ppc-static -cpu 7400):
checkasm h264dsp (loop_filter, loop_filter_intra) and h264chroma
(chroma_mc) show a real ALTIVEC: dispatch block and pass across 6 random
seeds; full checkasm suite 523/523 with no regressions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LCUwKztMy8skn2sLARXVo9
